<section class="page-hero"><span class="eyebrow">Capabilities</span><h1>Features</h1><p>PocketCat combines task and project workflows with optional Amazon Bedrock-powered assistance. Core work remains usable without AI; when enabled, model requests are handled server-side and subject to account access and usage controls.</p></section><section class="section"><div class="section-inner">
<article class="about-section"><span class="eyebrow">01</span><h2>Task management</h2><p>Tasks support Todo, In Progress and Completed states together with Low, Medium and High priorities. Due dates make deadlines visible and descriptions provide enough room for supporting details.</p><p>Task records are stored in MySQL and changes are immediately reflected in the workspace. Activity counters can also update the public landing page after a new task is created.</p></article>
<article class="about-section"><span class="eyebrow">02</span><h2>Notes and context</h2><p>Notes give users a place to record information that should remain available while work progresses. Pinning provides a simple way to surface important context.</p><p>The notes area is deliberately less formal than a document system. It works well for decisions, research snippets, meeting notes and ideas that need to stay close to active work.</p></article>
<article class="about-section"><span class="eyebrow">03</span><h2>Projects and milestones</h2><p>Projects organize related work around an outcome. Status and dates provide a simple planning layer, while tasks can be linked to the project.</p><p>Milestones provide another level of visibility for important checkpoints without forcing users into an overly complicated hierarchy.</p></article>
<article class="about-section"><span class="eyebrow">04</span><h2>Amazon Bedrock AI assistant</h2><p>The optional AI assistant connects to Amazon Bedrock for supported model workflows, including Converse and streaming responses where the selected model supports them. Administrators can configure a Bedrock API key or AWS IAM credentials, region and model identifier; a relay connection is also supported when deliberately configured.</p><p>Credentials and request signing are handled by the server, and saved secrets are encrypted at rest rather than exposed to frontend JavaScript. AI requests are checked against account access and usage allowances before the provider is called. Prompts may be processed by the configured AWS region and model, so users should avoid submitting information they are not authorized to share.</p></article>
<article class="about-section"><span class="eyebrow">05</span><h2>Search and administration</h2><p>Search brings tasks, notes and projects into a common discovery surface. Administrators get separate pages for users, security, database, email, AI, site settings and contact messages.</p><p>This division makes the application easier to operate as the number of accounts grows, while ordinary users remain focused on their own workspace.</p></article>
</div></section><section class="cta"><span class="eyebrow" style="color:#9db8ff">POCKETCAT</span><h2>Explore the workspace.</h2><p>See the product, create an account or contact the team when you are ready.</p><a class="btn" href="/signup/">Get Started</a></section><?php public_footer(); ?>